      "title": "Montage begins trial production of CXL 3.2 memory expansion chip, with Samsung and SK hynix completing initial validation - XenoSpectrum",
      "date": "2026-08-03",
      "source": "XenoSpectrum",
      "url": "https://xenospectrum.com/en/montage-cxl-3-2-trial-chip/",
      "summary": "Montage begins trial production of CXL 3.2 memory expansion chip, with Samsung and SK hynix completing initial validation XenoSpectrum",
      "body": "A CXL 3.2-compliant controller that expands server memory beyond the CPU has entered trial production. Chinese semiconductor design company Montage Technology (澜起科技) announced on July 30, 2026, the trial production of its memory expansion controller (MXC), the \"M88MX6852.\" The company describes it as an industry first.\nWhat matters in this announcement is less the headline figures—up to 64 GT/s and DDR5-8000—and more how far the product has progressed toward commercialization. The same model number began sampling to key customers as a CXL 3.1-compliant part back in September 2025. This time, Samsung Electronics and SK hynix have incorporated it into their next-generation CXL products and completed initial validation. What matters here is that trial production and initial validation on the memory maker side have come together. However, Montage has not disclosed the scale or yield of trial production, nor the timing of supply start to customers.\nA single chip bridging 64 GT/s CXL and DDR",
